# Everything is LF in the repository and LF in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# Two reasons, both load bearing. git_relay.py is executable and carries a shebang,
# so a CRLF checkout makes it fail with "bad interpreter" under Linux and WSL. And
# this checkout is routinely used from both Windows and WSL at once: Windows git
# commonly runs with core.autocrlf=true, which would rewrite line endings on one
# side and leave the other seeing every line as changed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Keep git from ever applying text conversion to these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gz binary
